From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] loader: wowbox64 as the x86 emulator on arm64

32-bit x86 programs on an arm64 Wine need a WoW64 CPU dll; the default
name, xtajit.dll, is Windows' own and Wine has none. Box64's wowbox64.dll
(package wowbox64) is it. The key has to exist before the 32-bit part of
the prefix is installed (Wow64Install runs syswow64\rundll32.exe, and
syswow64 is filled only while the prefix is bootstrapped), so it is in
PreInstall, which wineboot runs first in the native rundll32.

---
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 [PreInstall.ntarm64]
 WineFakeDlls=FakeDllsPreInstall
-AddReg=Wow64
+AddReg=Wow64,Wow64Arm64
 
 [PreInstall.Services]
 AddService=MountMgr,0x800,MountMgrService
@@ -1131,6 +1131,10 @@
 HKLM,%Control%\Windows,"CSDVersion",0x10003,0
 HKLM,%Control%\Session Manager\Environment,"OS",2,"Windows_NT"
 
+[Wow64Arm64]
+; x86 code runs in Box64's WoW64 build (wowbox64.dll)
+HKLM,Software\Microsoft\Wow64\x86,,,"wowbox64.dll"
+
 [Wow64]
 ; Wow6432Node symlinks
 HKLM,Software\Classes\Wow6432Node\AppId,"SymbolicLinkValue",0x60000,"\Registry\Machine\Software\Classes\AppId"
